    sections: [["Split by duration or by timestamps", "For a long recording, enter 300 seconds to create roughly five-minute parts; the final part may be shorter. For chapter boundaries, switch to timestamps and enter 0:30, 1:00. Cut points are sorted and aligned to nearby MP3 frames. The result list shows the actual boundaries before downloading."], ["What does no re-encoding mean?", "The splitter copies existing audio frames; it does not change bitrate, sample rate or channels, and it cannot restore detail already lost in the MP3. Frame boundaries and decoder dependencies mean this is not sample-accurate or guaranteed gapless editing. Listen to the beginning and end of each exported part."], ["Download on a phone or computer", "Preview any exported part, then download it individually or choose one ZIP containing all parts. A browser may save directly to Downloads instead of opening a dialog. Files remain on your device; memory, supported playback and ZIP size depend on your browser. Conversion, merging and fades are not included."]],
    editTitle: "How to Edit MP3 Online: Trim, Split, Preview and Save",
    editDescription: "Learn how to edit an MP3 in your browser: trim one excerpt or split it into multiple files, preview the result and save without re-encoding. Includes limitations.",
    editIntro: "Editing an MP3 can mean keeping one passage, making chapters, or changing the sound itself. Sonic Cutter handles trimming and splitting existing MP3 files locally. Volume changes, fades, mixing, noise removal and format conversion are not available here.",
    steps: [["Choose trim or split", "Use the audio cutter to keep one continuous excerpt. Open the MP3 splitter to keep the recording as several consecutive files. Both work with a local MP3; a protected music download is not made compatible by changing its extension."], ["Set the boundaries", "For trimming, drag the waveform handles or enter the start and end. For splitting, enter a duration in seconds or a comma-separated list such as 0:30, 1:00. The splitter keeps all parts, including the final remainder, and shows frame-aligned times."], ["Preview before saving", "In the cutter, preview the selected range. In the splitter, the preview plays the actual exported MP3 part. Listen for clipped words, the first note and the closing pause. MP3 decoder dependencies may affect the opening of a segment."], ["Save and check the result", "Save one clip, download individual parts, or use a ZIP for several parts. Find the file in browser Downloads or your device's Files app, and play it in another player if needed. The original file is unchanged; keep it for future edits."]],
